## 4.5 Design Direction

Avoid these clichés completely:

- No warm-cream background with a terracotta/clay accent and a big serif headline.
- No near-black background with a single neon-green or acid accent used everywhere.
- No hairline-rule "broadsheet" layout with dense newspaper columns.
- No centered hero with a gradient-blob background and a generic stock photo of unrelated smiling people.
- No numbered "01 / 02 / 03" feature cards unless there's a real sequence being described.
- No emoji in copy or UI, no generic icon-pack icons standing in for real photography.
- No filler marketing copy - "world-class," "premier," "unlock your potential," "passionate about delivering excellence." Every claim needs to be something you could actually back up from the snapshot in 4.2.

Also avoid: cartoon bugs, bug silhouettes, shield or checkmark badges, green "eco" leaf imagery, and anything that makes it look like a franchise.

### Palette (strictly monochrome, taken from the logo)

The logo is pure black on white. The site stays black and white. No accent colour. Define as CSS custom properties in `:root`:

| Token | Value | Why it earns its place |
|---|---|---|
| `--ink` | `#0B0B0B` | The logo black. Text, hero blocks, buttons. |
| `--paper` | `#FFFFFF` | The logo background. Main page colour. |
| `--fog` | `#F2F2F2` | Alternate section background so sections separate without lines. |
| `--graphite` | `#2A2A2A` | Hover and pressed states on black surfaces, footer detail. |
| `--ash` | `#6B6B6B` | Secondary text only. Check AA contrast on `--paper` and `--fog`. |
| `--rule` | `#D9D9D9` | The few dividers that exist. |

Contrast is the whole look: huge black blocks against clean white, with confident negative space. No gradients, no shadows heavier than a soft 1px-style lift on buttons.

### Typography

- **Display: Abril Fatface** (fallback `"Playfair Display"` 900, then Georgia). It matches the heavy, high-contrast serif of the RUSSELL&CO wordmark, so headings feel like part of the same brand. Use it for the H1, H2 and the ampersand.
- **Body and UI: Montserrat** (400, 500, 700, 800). It matches the bold geometric numerals of the phone number on their card. Use weight 800 for phone numbers.
- **Eyebrow labels:** Montserrat 500, uppercase, `letter-spacing: 0.4em`, small size. This copies the spaced-out PEST SOLUTIONS line in the logo. Use it for section labels.
- Fluid type with `clamp()`. Headlines tight (`line-height: 0.95` to `1.05`), body relaxed (`1.6`).

### Signature element (spend the boldness here, stay disciplined everywhere else)

**The phone number as a poster.** On the home page hero, `0433 355 980` is set at enormous scale in Montserrat 800, filling most of the width, exactly like the business card. Above it the eyebrow line `LICENSED PEST CONTROL`, below it the licence line `LICENCE NO: PMT010768922` in regular weight. The number is a tap-to-call link. Everything else on the site is quiet and clean around that one loud moment.

### Motion

Sparse and deliberate only: a short fade-and-rise reveal on sections as they scroll in, and a clean colour-invert on button hover. Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` fully: when set, no animation or transition at all, not just reduced. No parallax, no marquee, no animated counters.

### Quality floor (always)

Fully responsive down to 360px wide, visible keyboard focus states on every interactive element (a 3px outline with offset, never removed), real descriptive alt text on every image, semantic HTML5 throughout (`header`, `nav`, `main`, `section`, `footer`, exactly one `h1` per page, correct heading order). Minimum 44px tap targets for call and SMS buttons.

