## 4.8 Copy and Tone

Write like a tradesperson who runs his own business, not an agency. Plain, active, specific. Short paragraphs. No adjective stacking. No exclamation marks. Every claim traces back to 4.2.

Bad generic line: "We deliver world-class pest solutions tailored to your unique needs with unmatched professionalism."

Good line for this business: "Licensed pest control across South East Queensland. Call or text Darren on 0433 355 980."

Button language: "Call", "Text", "Email". Not "Get started", not "Learn more", not "Contact us today".

No em dashes anywhere (see 4.1). Use a full stop or a comma instead.

