## 4.9 main.js Required Functionality

- Accessible mobile nav toggle: button with `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls`, keyboard operable, closes on outside click and on Escape, returns focus to the toggle on close.
- Smooth scroll for on-page anchors (the services anchors), disabled when `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce`.
- Scroll-triggered reveal using `IntersectionObserver`. When reduced motion is set, content simply shows with no animation. Content must also be visible if JavaScript fails (add the hidden state only via a class set by JS).
- **Sticky mobile call bar:** on viewports under 768px, a fixed bottom bar with two equal buttons, Call and Text. Show it after the user scrolls past the hero. Hide it on the contact page, where those actions are already the whole page. Add bottom padding to the footer so the bar never covers content.
- Active nav state for the current page via `aria-current="page"`.
- **No form handling.** There is no backend and no form. Contact is click-to-call, SMS, email and socials only.
- No libraries. No console errors.

